<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4717" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăvītus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		avus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a grandfather</i>, <i>coming from a grandfather</i>, <i>ancestral.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paternae atque avitae possessiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Agr. 2, 30, 81</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bona paterna et avita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Cael. 14, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res patrita et avita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Verr. 1, 5, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patrita illa et avita philosophia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tusc. 1, 19, 45</span></i>
			: avitus ac patritus mos, Varr. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. p. 161, 5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">leges avitae et patritae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hospitium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 13, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">divitiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					68, 121</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 6, 79</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae (pallium, sudarium etc.) palam soles
					habere tamquam avita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					25, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 169</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6, 650</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 12, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cellae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 37, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regnum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Imp. Pomp. 8, 12</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanguis, Prep. 3, 19, 37: nomen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					6, 239</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">umbrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.1, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nobilitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					2, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 35, 58, § 117</span></i>
			 et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b> to animals: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">asinus fortitudinem celeritatemque avitam
					refert,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					6, 37, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">color,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 6, 37, 4, § 7</span></i>
			.—In gen., <i>very old</i> or <i>ancient</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">merum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 2, 695</span></i>
			.—<i>Comp.</i> and <i>sup.</i> not found; cf. Neue, Formenl. II. p.
			230.—* <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăvītë</span></b> ;, <i>from
				ancient times</i>, <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Val.
			39</span></i> dub.</div>
